  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company operates in a bifurcated consumer credit environment—a K-shaped economy where lower-income borrowers face mounting strain, as evident from rising delinquencies. Despite this, core lending operations are growing, with record origination volumes and expanding loan balances, suggesting robust demand and successful outreach to credit-worthy segments. The macro backdrop remains Headwinds-driven, with inflation and employment divergence creating a need for careful risk selection, yet the business is exhibiting resilience rather than broad-based deterioration.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership demonstrates disciplined underwriting and cost control, achieving historically low operating expense ratios while still investing in the business. Capital allocation skews shareholder-friendly, returning cash through a meaningful dividend yield, and the market rewards the team’s credibility in balancing growth with credit stewardship. The narrative portrays management as adept at steering through a volatile cycle, prioritizing portfolio quality and operational efficiency without retreating from its core market.",
